#: ../../chapter02.rst:3
msgid "2 Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:5
msgid "Login to your |prodname| web portal ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:9
msgid "Click the **User Icon (1)** then select the **Download Client (2)** button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:13
msgid "You will then see the **\"Download Native Clients\"** page. Choose the **Installer Package (3)** for your system. Click the Downloads link on the top-right of the window and double-click on the **Mac Client .dmg file (4)** to start the Cloud Drive Installer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:17
msgid "Double click on the **\"Cloud Drive\" volume (1)**. Click **\"Continue\" (2)**, then **\"Agree\" (3)** to the License Agreement to continue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:21
msgid "Select **\"Continue\" (4)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:23
msgid "Enter username and password for the MAC machine and select **\"Install Software\"**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:27
msgid "Select 'Continue'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:29
msgid "Once the software is installed, on the MAC machine go to ``Finder`` > ``Applications`` and double click on the **\"Cloud Drive Mac Client\"** icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:31
msgid "Login to the Cloud Drive using your |prodname| \"User Name\" and \"Password\". Ensure that the Access point is set to the proper domain or IP address. and click **\"Login\"**. These credentials will authorize your Cloud Drive Client and connect it to your |prodname| user account."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:35
msgid "Once you have logged in, you can see the Cloud drive as a mounted Volume in the Finder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:39
msgid "The cloud drive icon  will appear on the MAC machine's  main screen. You can also double click on the icon to access the cloud drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:46
msgid "Primary Use Cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:48
msgid "Collaborative access to the Cloud Drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:50
msgid "The Drive based random access is one of the primary way of accessing files and folders in the cloud drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:52
msgid "Syncing local folders to the Cloud Drive for remote access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:54
msgid "Another primary use case is users want to continue to work in a local folder, and then attach that folder to the |prodname| account so the content of the folder (or folders) will be synchronized in a 2-way fashion between the local Mac folder and the remote |prodname| folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:56
msgid "After the installation is completed, a system tray icon will appear that allows you to open your |prodname| Drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../chapter02.rst:60
msgid "you can access the managemnt console for |prodname| Drive and you can also perform a quick check of your system status."
msgstr ""
